+# R51 — E2LB fallback binding isolation
+
+## Finding
+
+R50 built the persistent fallback key from `receiverBinding.orEmpty()` plus receiver capability identity. `ReceiverDetectionRuntime.binding(address)` returns null until the private `ReceiverConfigurationStore` has loaded, and also returns null for an unavailable/invalid Bluetooth address. In that case, two receiver instances reporting the same normalized capabilities would derive the same persistent fingerprint from the empty binding. This violates the stated per-receiver isolation guarantee.
+
+## Change
+
+- `ReceiverFingerprint.e2lbAvailabilityFingerprint()` now requires the 64-character lowercase HMAC binding produced by `ReceiverConfigurationStore.binding()`.
+- `Iap2SenderSession` reads and stores fallback state only when that stable binding exists.
+- With no stable binding, R51 preserves the user's explicitly selected DUAL_GROUP/SINGLE_GROUP shape for the current attempt but does not read or persist cross-attempt automatic fallback state.
+- `CompatibilityPrefs` validates the exact `e2lb4300_<64 lowercase hex>` key shape on both read and write.
+- No raw Bluetooth address, display name, or untrusted string is used as a preference key.
+
+## Regression coverage
+
+- null, blank, raw MAC, short digest and non-hex binding are rejected;
+- a valid private binding yields a deterministic E2LB fingerprint;
+- two distinct bindings with identical receiver capabilities produce distinct fingerprints;
+- malformed fingerprint values are rejected by the key validator;
+- the pure fallback-selection policy refuses to activate a remembered fallback without E2LB opt-in, context, and a valid receiver fingerprint;
+- a fake SharedPreferences integration harness verifies malformed-key rejection, valid persistence, and manual-toggle reset.
+
+## Non-claims / remaining blockers
+
+This is an isolation and persistence-safety fix only. It does not prove that `DUAL_GROUP` caused the peer iAP2 restart, does not implement MFi certificate/signature verification, and does not establish that `SINGLE_GROUP` will produce 0x4301. Full Android Gradle gate, APK build, and E2LB real-vehicle validation remain required.
